*HPDC=E2=80=9915 - Call for Participation and Posters**
**http://www.hpdc.org/2015/**
*
/*NEWS:*//*
*//*- Poster/Abstract submission deadline: May 8th, 2015*//*
*//*- Early Registration deadline: May 18th, 2015*//*
*//*- Conference dates: June 15th-19th, 2015*//*
*//*    - Keynote: Allen D. Malony*//*
*//*    - HPDC Achievement Award winner: Ewa Deelman*/

HPDC=E2=80=9915, the 24th International ACM Symposium on High Performance=
=20
Parallel and Distributed Computing, will be held in Portland, Oregon,=20
June 15-19, 2015. HPDC=E2=80=9915 will be part of FCRC=E2=80=9915, ACM=E2=
=80=99s Federated=20
Computing Research Conference, hosting no less than 13 top-level=20
conferences and symposia, along with an exciting program of joint=20
keynote lectures, opening on the evening of June 14th with the A.M.=20
Turing Award Lecture, delivered by the 2014 award winner, Michael=20
Stonebreaker.

HPDC is hosting a total of seven workshops on June 15 and 16. The main=20
HPDC conference will run from June 17 to 19, featuring 30 presentations=20
of papers and short papers, two keynotes, and a poster session. This=20
year=E2=80=99s HPDC keynote presentations will be given by Allen D. Malon=
y and=20
this year=E2=80=99s HPDC Achievement Award winner, Ewa Deelman.

Please see http://www.hpdc.org/2015/ for details. Registration (via=20
FCRC) is open now. Deadline for discounted, early registration is May=20
18, 2015. Travel grants for students attending a US institution are=20
available, sponsored by NSF.

*Call for posters:**
*
HPDC'15 will feature a poster session that will provide the right=20
environment for lively and informal discussions on various high=20
performance parallel and distributed computing topics. There will be a=20
"poster session and reception" on Wednesday, 6-8 pm. Posters can remain=20
on display during the three days of the HPDC main conference (Wednesday=20
to Friday). We invite all potential authors to submit their contribution=20
to this poster session in the form of a two-page PDF abstract (we=20
recommend using the ACM Proceedings style, and fonts not smaller than 10=20
point). Posters may be accompanied by practical demonstrations.=20
Abstracts must be submitted by May 8th 2015 through=20
https://www.easychair.org/conferences/?conf=3Dhpdc15posters. For any=20
questions about the submission, selection, and presentation of the=20
accepted posters, please contact the Posters Chair - Ana-Maria Oprescu=20
<amo@cs.vu.nl>, Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam, The Netherlands.




--=20
